      "message": "Hi, sorry again for the slow review!\n\nI\u0027m a bit nit-picky on the naming in my comments, but this is because I have seen this code evolve and deteriorate into really confusing naming after a series of rewrites (most of which I did myself). It\u0027s not your fault, but I suggest that you do a few CLs preceding this one to do some renaming and prepare the code to the introduction of on-device paths. There is symmetry between on-host and on-device paths, so there should be symmetry in the names as well.\n\nSo, I suggest:\n- first prepare a few CLs that rename various image paths to have the word \"OnHost\" in them (see the comments below that spot particular names that should be changed)\n- then do this CL that introduces symmetric \"OnDevice\" paths\n\nThe other general request is, as you add more logic to handle dexpreopt of unbundled partition, please add extended comments that explain it. You can have one long comment some place and refer to it in other places to avoid duplication. It is also fine to do in a follow-up CL.\n\nFinally, there is a need for some reproducible way to test your work: either a sequence of shell commands or a script that you would mention in the \u0027Test:\u0027 field. I\u0027m assuming here that you\u0027ll want to test the same thing in many commits (like the logcat grepping command that I run to see rejected dexpreopt at boot).\n",
